<title>SWEDEN: S&amp;P says possible Swedish upgrade depends on debt.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P says possible Swedish upgrade depends on debt.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. credit ratings agency Standard &amp; Poor's (S&amp;P) said on Friday that an upgrade or even a positive outlook for the Kingdom of Sweden ratings was contingent upon substantial progress in lowering the country's fiscal debt programme.</p>
<p>S&amp;P revised its ratings for the Kingdom of Sweden to stable from negative.  </p>
<p>Sweden's fiscal debt burden is at the high end of the range for AA rated sovereigns, S&amp;P said in a statement.</p>
<p>It affirmed Sweden's AA+ longterm foreign currency credit rating, its AAA longterm local currency credit rating and its A-1+ shortterm debt ratings.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
